   <narrative xml:lang="EN">United Nations Industrial Development Organization</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Improving agro-industrial capacity for rural revitalization in Chengbu, China</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">UNIDO was implementing the Project #Improving industrial capacity for poverty reduction in Chengbu, China# during July 2018 to June 2021 to reduce poverty in Chengbu Miao Autonomous County, Hunan Province, China through increasing the utilization of agro-based raw materials and improve the industrial capacity for producing goods with higher value added, for the contribution to China#s national poverty alleviation strategies and policies. The Project implementation reached the outcomes including upgraded technology and improved quality in bamboo and dairy products, improved innovative design capability of ethnic cultural products, and increased local capacity on through e-commerce. From the impact reached by the Project, the local counterparts in Chengbu invited UNIDO to develop a second-phase project to continue the support and contribution to improving capacities for developing agricultural value chains, facilitating job creation and income generation for agro-practitioners, and supporting local governmental agencies to advance their supervision capacities and service provision, which also has received welcoming message from the project donor, i.e. China Ministry of Commerce, for their further endorsement and support.</narrative>
  </description>
